    "metaDescription": "Answers to the most common SR-22 insurance questions: cost, timeline, non-owner policies, and more. Call Tidewater SR22 Virginia Beach at (757) 960-7569.",
    "contentHtml": "<h1>Frequently Asked Questions About SR-22 Insurance</h1>\n<p>Here are the questions Virginia Beach and Virginia drivers ask us most often about SR-22 insurance. If you don't see your question below, our <a href=\"/contact-us/\">Contact Us</a> page connects you directly with a specialist.</p>\n<h2>Is an SR-22 a type of insurance?</h2>\n<p>No. An SR-22 is a certificate your insurance company files with the DMV proving you carry the state's required minimum liability coverage. Learn more on our <a href=\"/what-is-sr22/\">financial responsibility certificate guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Why do I need an SR-22?</h2>\n<p>Virginia typically requires an SR-22 filing after an uninsured motor vehicle suspension, unsatisfied accident judgment, failure to provide insurance proof, or certain serious traffic convictions. (Note that DUI convictions in Virginia typically require an FR-44 filing with higher limits). If you're unsure why you specifically were flagged, <a href=\"https://www.dmv.virginia.gov/businesses/insurance/certifications\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the Virginia DMV</a> can confirm the exact reason tied to your record.</p>\n<h2>How long do I have to carry an SR-22 in Virginia?</h2>\n<p>The required period in Virginia is typically three continuous years. It's critical to maintain continuous coverage during that entire window &mdash; a lapse can restart the clock.</p>\n<h2>What happens if my SR-22 policy lapses?</h2>\n<p>Your insurer is required to notify the DMV if your policy lapses or is canceled. That notification triggers another license suspension and restarts your required filing period, so it's important to never miss a payment.</p>\n<h2>Do I need an SR-22 if I don't own a car?</h2>\n<p>Yes. Virginia requires the filing regardless of vehicle ownership. If you don't own a car, a non-owner SR-22 policy satisfies the requirement, usually at a lower cost than a standard owner policy. See our <a href=\"/non-owners-sr22-insurance/\">no-car SR-22 insurance solutions</a> page for details.</p>\n<h2>How much does SR-22 insurance cost?</h2>\n<p>Cost varies significantly based on your driving history, the violation involved, your age, and which insurer you choose. Because rates differ so much between carriers, getting a specific quote is the only reliable way to know your actual cost &mdash; call <a href=\"tel:+17579607569\">(757) 960-7569</a> and we'll give you a straight number.</p>\n<h2>Will my rates go back to normal once the SR-22 period ends?</h2>\n<p>Often, yes &mdash; once your required filing period ends and your driving record improves, standard insurance rates typically become available again. Maintaining a clean record and continuous coverage during your SR-22 period helps your rates normalize faster.</p>\n<h2>Can I switch insurance companies while on an SR-22?</h2>\n<p>Yes, but you need to make sure there's no gap in coverage during the switch, and your new insurer needs to file a new SR-22 certificate with the DMV before or as your old policy ends. We handle this transition carefully to avoid any lapse.</p>\n<h2>Does SR-22 insurance cover motorcycles?</h2>\n<p>Yes. Motorcycle riders who require a financial responsibility certification under Virginia law may also need an SR-22 filing before their license is reinstated. Motorcycle SR-22 policies are generally less expensive than auto policies, though pricing still depends on your record and the bike you ride.</p>\n<h2>How fast can I get my SR-22 filed?</h2>\n<p>Many drivers can get a policy bound and the certificate filed electronically within a single business day. For the full process, see our <a href=\"/how-to-get-an-sr22-in-virginia-beach/\">Virginia Beach driver licensing guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Do you serve my area?</h2>\n<p>Tidewater SR22 Insurance Virginia Beach serves all of Hampton Roads and Coastal Virginia, including Norfolk, Chesapeake, Newport News, Hampton, Portsmouth, Suffolk, Williamsburg, Poquoson, Smithfield, and Yorktown.</p>\n<h2>Can I drive at all while my SR-22 filing is being processed?</h2>\n<p>Generally, no &mdash; if your license is currently suspended, you shouldn't drive until it's officially reinstated and your SR-22 has been accepted by the DMV. Driving while suspended can add new violations to your record and further extend your required filing period, so it's worth the short wait to get everything filed properly first.</p>\n<h2>Can I get an SR-22 the same day my license was suspended?</h2>\n<p>Often, yes. If you already know which insurer you want to work with and have your driver's license information ready, many drivers can get a policy quoted, purchased, and filed with the DMV within the same business day.</p>\n<h2>What is the difference between an SR-22 and an FR-44 in Virginia?</h2>\n<p>In Virginia, an SR-22 certifies standard minimum liability limits ($50,000/$100,000/$25,000) typically following uninsured suspensions or judgments. An FR-44 is required for DUI/DWI convictions and requires double the liability coverage ($100,000/$300,000/$50,000).</p>\n<h2>Still Have Questions?</h2>\n<p>We'd rather you ask than guess. Visit us at 513 19th St ste 110, Virginia Beach, VA 23451, United States or reach out any time and we'll give you a clear, honest answer about your specific situation.</p>\n<p>Call Tidewater SR22 Insurance Virginia Beach today at <a href=\"tel:+17579607569\">(757) 960-7569</a> for a free, no-pressure SR-22 quote. We answer questions fast and file paperwork faster.</p>",
